steps:
  eyebrow: How it works
  h2: Survey, price, approve, send.
  intro: One chain of records. Nothing is typed twice between the surveyor, the sales team and the approver.
  items:
    - h: Survey on site
      p: A surveyor is assigned a booked visit and fills the survey on a phone. It captures location, roof, electrical and structural sections, up to nine photo categories, and a recommendation.
      path: ["Booked", "On site", "Completed"]
    - h: Feasibility verdict
      p: Every completed survey carries a verdict of go, conditional go or no go with a reason, plus a suggested system size and project type.
      path: ["Survey", "Verdict", "Recommended kW"]
    - h: Priced quotation
      p: A bill of materials is generated from rules on your catalogue, such as quantity per kW, panel count, string count and cable length, with GST on each line.
      path: ["Catalogue", "BOM rules", "Priced lines"]
    - h: Approve and send
      p: The quotation is submitted, approved or rejected by a person with that permission, and only an approved quotation can be sent to the customer.
      path: ["Draft", "Approval", "Sent"]
features:
  eyebrow: What it does
  h2: Quotations your team can trust and your owner can control.
  items:
    - h: Survey sections for solar
      p: Location, roof, electrical, structural, recommendation and customer interaction are captured as structured sections, and you can set up survey templates.
      li: ["Photos in nine categories", "Location captured with the survey"]
    - h: Catalogue-driven BOM
      p: Rules on each catalogue item decide quantities, so a 5 kW quote and a 50 kW quote are built the same careful way.
      li: ["Fixed, per kW, panel count, string and cable rules", "GST rate on every line"]
    - h: Approval queue
      p: Quotations wait in a queue for the people allowed to approve or reject them. A quote that is not approved cannot go out.
      li: ["Submit, approve, reject", "Rejection reasons stay on the record"]
    - h: Revisions with history
      p: Change a price or a size and create a revision. Each version and the reason for it stay on the quotation timeline.
      li: ["Version numbers per enquiry", "Events logged on the quotation"]
    - h: Internal costing by permission
      p: Margins and base costs show only to people with the internal costing permission. Everyone else sees the customer prices they need.
      li: ["Cost and margin hidden by default", "Controlled by role"]
    - h: Customer proposal
      p: A proposal PDF presents project cost, subsidy, net payable, estimated generation, savings, payback and environmental impact, with your terms.
      li: ["Subsidy and net payable", "Savings, payback and generation"]
